# -*- mode:org; mode:auto-fill; fill-column:80; coding:utf-8; -*-
#+title: dawa-tts - Lightning-fast Multilingual TTS for Emacs
#+author: Sangjee Dondrub

* Overview

*dawa-tts* is an Emacs dynamic module that brings ultra-fast multilingual
text-to-speech synthesis to Emacs using the [[https://github.com/supertone-inc/supertonic][Supertonic TTS engine v3]]. It
provides on-device speech synthesis with zero latency and complete privacy.

* Features

- *Blazingly Fast*: Generates speech up to 167× faster than real-time
  (< 0.2s for typical sentences)
- *Multilingual*: Supports 32 languages with automatic detection
- *Ultra Lightweight*: Only 66M parameter model
- *On-Device*: Complete privacy, no cloud, no API calls
- *Multiple Voices*: 10 voice styles (M1-M5 male, F1-F5 female)
- *Natural Text Handling*: Seamlessly handles numbers, dates, currency,
  abbreviations
- *Progressive Chunk Highlighting*: Highlights text chunks as they're being
  spoken with language-aware timing
- *Configurable*: Adjust inference steps, speed, voice styles, and highlight
  colors

* Supported Languages (33)

Arabic (ar), Bulgarian (bg), Chinese (zh), Croatian (hr), Czech (cs), Danish (da),
Dutch (nl), English (en), Estonian (et), Finnish (fi), French (fr), German (de),
Greek (el), Hindi (hi), Hungarian (hu), Indonesian (id), Italian (it), Japanese
(ja), Korean (ko), Latvian (lv), Lithuanian (lt), Polish (pl), Portuguese (pt),
Romanian (ro), Russian (ru), Slovak (sk), Slovenian (sl), Spanish (es), Swedish
(sv), Turkish (tr), Ukrainian (uk), Vietnamese (vi), Language-agnostic (na)

*Note*: Chinese (zh) is automatically detected and internally mapped to
language-agnostic mode ("na") for optimal Supertonic v3 processing.

* Performance

On M4 Pro (CPU):
- *Speed*: 0.12-0.16 seconds for typical sentences
- *Throughput*: 1000+ characters/second
- *Real-time Factor*: 0.012 (generates 1 second of audio in 0.012 seconds)

* Installation

** Prerequisites

1. *Emacs 25.1+* with dynamic module support
2. *Dependencies* (macOS):

#+begin_src shell
brew install cmake nlohmann-json onnxruntime git-lfs
git lfs install
#+end_src

** Clone and Setup

#+begin_src shell
cd ~/.emacs.d/etc/lisp/
git clone <this-repo> dawa-tts
#+end_src

** Emacs Configuration

Add to your =init.el=:

#+begin_src elisp
(add-to-list 'load-path "~/.emacs.d/etc/lisp/dawa-tts/")
(require 'dawa-tts)
#+end_src

*The module will automatically compile on first load!*

When you first =(require 'dawa-tts)=, Emacs will:
1. Check if the module needs compilation
2. Ask for confirmation: "dawa-tts module needs compilation. Compile now?"
3. Run CMake to build the module
4. Download assets if needed (via CMake)
5. Load the compiled module

** Using use-package

If you prefer using =use-package= for configuration:

#+begin_src elisp
(use-package dawa-tts
  :load-path "~/.emacs.d/etc/lisp/dawa-tts/"
  :commands (dawa-tts-speak
             dawa-tts-speak-word
             dawa-tts-speak-sentence
             dawa-tts-speak-region
             dawa-tts-speak-buffer
             dawa-tts-stop
             dawa-tts-load-voice
             dawa-tts-toggle-highlight)
  :init
  ;; Optional: Set default voice before loading
  (setq dawa-tts-voice-style "F1")
  :config
  ;; Adjust synthesis quality (2-10, default: 5)
  (setq dawa-tts-inference-steps 5)
  ;; Adjust speech speed (0.5-2.0, default: 1.05)
  (setq dawa-tts-speed 1.05)
  ;; Enable text highlighting (default: t)
  (setq dawa-tts-highlight-text t)

  ;; Optional: Set keybindings
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s s") 'dawa-tts-speak)
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s w") 'dawa-tts-speak-word)
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s r") 'dawa-tts-speak-region)
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s b") 'dawa-tts-speak-buffer)
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s q") 'dawa-tts-stop)
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s v") 'dawa-tts-load-voice)
  (global-set-key (kbd "C-c s h") 'dawa-tts-toggle-highlight))
#+end_src

*Note:* The module will automatically compile on first load, even when loaded via
=use-package=. You'll be prompted to confirm compilation if the module is
missing or out of date.

** Manual Building (Optional)

If you prefer to build manually before loading:

#+begin_src shell
cd ~/.emacs.d/etc/lisp/dawa-tts/
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
cmake --build . --config Release
#+end_src

Or use the interactive command:

#+begin_src elisp
M-x dawa-tts-compile
#+end_src

* Usage

** Basic Usage

#+begin_src elisp
;; Speak text directly (auto-detects language)
(dawa-tts-speak "Hello from Emacs")
(dawa-tts-speak "你好世界")  ; Chinese
(dawa-tts-speak "안녕하세요")  ; Korean

;; Force specific language
(dawa-tts-speak "Bonjour le monde" "fr")
(dawa-tts-speak "Hola mundo" "es")

;; Speak current word (highlights the word)
(dawa-tts-speak-word)

;; Speak selected region (progressively highlights chunks)
(dawa-tts-speak-region)

;; Speak entire buffer (progressively highlights chunks)
(dawa-tts-speak-buffer)

;; Stop playback
(dawa-tts-stop)
#+end_src

** Language Configuration

#+begin_src elisp
;; Set buffer-local language (overrides auto-detection)
M-x dawa-tts-lang-set RET ko RET  ; Force Korean

;; Clear language override (use auto-detection)
M-x dawa-tts-lang-clear

;; Toggle auto-detection on/off
M-x dawa-tts-lang-toggle-auto-detect

;; Set default language (used when auto-detection fails)
(setq dawa-tts-lang-default "en")  ; English (default)
(setq dawa-tts-lang-default "na")  ; Language-agnostic mode

;; Disable auto-detection (always use default)
(setq dawa-tts-lang-auto-detect nil)
#+end_src

** Voice Configuration

#+begin_src elisp
;; List available voices
(dawa-tts-list-voices)
;; => ("M1" "M2" "M3" "M4" "M5" "F1" "F2" "F3" "F4" "F5")

;; Switch voice interactively
M-x dawa-tts-load-voice RET M2 RET

;; Or programmatically
(dawa-tts-load-voice "F3")

;; Set default voice
(setq dawa-tts-voice-style "M1")
#+end_src

** Advanced Configuration

#+begin_src elisp
;; Adjust synthesis quality (2-10, default: 5)
;; Higher = better quality but slower
(setq dawa-tts-inference-steps 7)

;; Adjust speech speed (0.5-2.0, default: 1.05)
(setq dawa-tts-speed 1.2)

;; Disable auto-play (just generate WAV files)
(setq dawa-tts-auto-play nil)

;; Custom audio player (Linux)
(setq dawa-tts-player-command "aplay")

;; Disable text highlighting
(setq dawa-tts-highlight-text nil)

;; Customize highlight face
(set-face-attribute 'dawa-tts-highlight-face nil
                    :background "light blue"
                    :foreground "black")
#+end_src

** Text Highlighting

The progressive chunk highlighting feature provides visual feedback during speech
synthesis:

- *Single word* (=dawa-tts-speak-word=): Highlights the word being spoken
- *Single sentence* (=dawa-tts-speak-sentence=): Highlights the sentence being spoken
- *Region/Buffer* (=dawa-tts-speak-region=, =dawa-tts-speak-buffer=):
  Progressively highlights text chunks as they're spoken, synchronized with audio
  playback. Chunk-based highlighting provides better accuracy with language-aware
  duration estimation (CJK languages use 120-char chunks, others use 300-char chunks).
- Highlighting automatically disappears when playback finishes or is stopped

Toggle highlighting: =M-x dawa-tts-toggle-highlight=

** Keybindings (Example)

#+begin_src elisp
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s s") 'dawa-tts-speak)
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s w") 'dawa-tts-speak-word)
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s r") 'dawa-tts-speak-region)
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s b") 'dawa-tts-speak-buffer)
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s q") 'dawa-tts-stop)
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s v") 'dawa-tts-load-voice)
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c s h") 'dawa-tts-toggle-highlight)
#+end_src

* Architecture

#+begin_example
┌─────────────────────┐
│   dawa-tts.el       │  ← Emacs Lisp interface
│  (User commands)    │
└──────────┬──────────┘
           │ require
┌──────────▼──────────┐
│ dawa-tts-module.dylib│  ← C++ dynamic module
│ (Emacs ↔ C++ bridge)│
└──────────┬──────────┘
           │ calls
┌──────────▼──────────┐
│  Supertonic C++     │  ← TTS engine (lib/supertonic.cpp)
│  TTS Implementation │
└──────────┬──────────┘
           │ uses
┌──────────▼──────────┐
│  ONNX Runtime       │  ← ML inference
│  (4 neural models)  │
└─────────────────────┘
#+end_example

* File Structure

#+begin_example
dawa-tts/
├── Makefile                 # Build automation
├── CMakeLists.txt           # CMake build configuration
├── dawa-tts.el              # Main Emacs Lisp interface
├── dawa-tts-lang.el         # Language detection (32 languages)
├── dawa-tts-chunk.el        # Smart text chunking
├── dawa-tts-module.cpp      # C++ dynamic module
├── dawa-tts-module.dylib    # Compiled module (macOS)
├── test-dawa-tts.el         # ERT test suite (33 tests)
├── TESTING.md               # Testing guide
├── lib/                     # Supertonic TTS library
│   ├── supertonic.cpp       # Core TTS implementation (v3)
│   └── supertonic.h         # TTS API headers
├── build/                   # CMake build directory (gitignored)
└── assets/                  # Models and voices (auto-downloaded, gitignored)
    ├── onnx/                # ONNX model files (260MB total)
    │   ├── duration_predictor.onnx
    │   ├── text_encoder.onnx
    │   ├── vector_estimator.onnx
    │   ├── vocoder.onnx
    │   ├── tts.json
    │   └── unicode_indexer.json
    └── voice_styles/        # Voice embeddings (10 voices)
        ├── F1.json
        ├── F2.json
        ⋮
        └── M5.json
#+end_example

* Development

** Building from Source

#+begin_src shell
# Using Makefile (recommended)
make build          # Build the module
make clean          # Clean build artifacts
make rebuild        # Clean and rebuild
make check          # Check if module exists

# Manual build
cd build
rm ./*
cmake ..
cmake --build . --config Release
#+end_src

** Testing

#+begin_src shell
# Run all ERT tests (33 tests)
make test

# Run interactive multilingual test
make test-interactive

# Or manually
emacs -Q --batch -l dawa-tts-lang.el -l dawa-tts-chunk.el \
  -l test-dawa-tts.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit

# Interactive test
emacs -Q -l dawa-tts.el -l test-dawa-tts.el \
  --eval "(dawa-tts-test-multilingual)"
#+end_src

See =TESTING.md= for comprehensive testing guide.

** Troubleshooting

*** Module won't load

#+begin_src shell
# Check if Emacs has module support
emacs --batch --eval "(message \"%s\" module-file-suffix)"
# Should output: .dylib (macOS) or .so (Linux)
#+end_src

*** ONNX Runtime errors

#+begin_src shell
# Verify ONNX Runtime installation
brew list onnxruntime
ls -la /opt/homebrew/lib/libonnxruntime.dylib
#+end_src

*** Missing models

Assets are automatically downloaded during CMake configuration. To manually
download:

#+begin_src shell
git clone https://huggingface.co/Supertone/supertonic assets
cd assets
git lfs pull
#+end_src

* API Reference

** Interactive Commands

- =dawa-tts-speak= - Synthesize and speak text
- =dawa-tts-speak-word= - Speak word at point (with highlighting)
- =dawa-tts-speak-sentence= - Speak sentence at point (with highlighting)
- =dawa-tts-speak-region= - Speak selected region (with progressive highlighting)
- =dawa-tts-speak-buffer= - Speak entire buffer (with progressive highlighting)
- =dawa-tts-stop= - Stop current playback and remove highlight
- =dawa-tts-load-voice= - Switch voice style
- =dawa-tts-toggle-highlight= - Toggle text highlighting on/off
- =dawa-tts-lang-set= - Set buffer-local language override
- =dawa-tts-lang-clear= - Clear buffer-local language override
- =dawa-tts-lang-toggle-auto-detect= - Toggle automatic language detection
- =dawa-tts-init= - Initialize TTS engine (auto-called)
- =dawa-tts-benchmark= - Run performance benchmark
- =dawa-tts-cleanup-temp-files= - Clean up temporary WAV files

** Customization Variables

- =dawa-tts-voice-style= - Default voice (default: "F1")
- =dawa-tts-inference-steps= - Quality/speed tradeoff (default: 5)
- =dawa-tts-speed= - Speech speed multiplier (default: 1.05)
- =dawa-tts-auto-play= - Auto-play generated audio (default: t)
- =dawa-tts-highlight-text= - Highlight text being spoken (default: t)
- =dawa-tts-lang-default= - Default language code (default: "en")
- =dawa-tts-lang-auto-detect= - Auto-detect text language (default: t)
- =dawa-tts-assets-dir= - Path to models and voices
- =dawa-tts-player-command= - Audio player command (default: "afplay")

** Faces

- =dawa-tts-highlight-face= - Face for highlighting spoken text (default: yellow
  background)

** Module Functions (Low-level)

- =(dawa-tts-module-init ONNX-DIR)= - Initialize ONNX Runtime
- =(dawa-tts-module-load-voice VOICE-PATH)= - Load voice JSON
- =(dawa-tts-module-synthesize TEXT LANG STEPS SPEED OUTPUT-PATH)= - Generate WAV
- =(dawa-tts-module-list-voices VOICE-DIR)= - List voice files
- =(dawa-tts-module-cleanup)= - Clean up resources

* Performance Tips

1. *Use fewer inference steps* for speed: =(setq dawa-tts-inference-steps 2)=
2. *Increase speech speed*: =(setq dawa-tts-speed 1.3)=
3. *Disable auto-play* for batch processing: =(setq dawa-tts-auto-play nil)=
4. *Keep the engine initialized* - first synthesis takes ~1s (loads models),
   subsequent ones are ~0.1s

* Known Issues

- Mutex cleanup warning on exit (non-critical, synthesis works correctly)
- Long texts (>300 chars) are automatically chunked with 0.3s silence

